From a9b0be425783c336fd1e2105fdcfe74d8e8a10d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:09:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] rk3326: do not request the DSI HS clock before an LPM
 panel is initialised

The XiFan RF35H panel (generic-dsi, flags 0xe03: video, burst, no EOT,
non-continuous clock, LPM) stays dark when dw-mipi-dsi asserts
PHY_TXREQUESTCLKHS before the panel's init sequence. For panels that
take their init in low power mode over a non-continuous clock lane,
power the controller up without the clock request; atomic_enable
requests it once the panel is ready. All RK3326 panels in the tree
declare both flags, so they all take this path, which is the sequence
the RF35H already boots with on other distributions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019W6m4A3E7pevQ1bs91jPmM
---
 ...si-lpm-panel-no-hs-clock-before-init.patch | 47 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 47 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 board/batocera/rockchip/rk3326/linux_patches/103-dw-mipi-dsi-lpm-panel-no-hs-clock-before-init.patch

diff --git a/board/batocera/rockchip/rk3326/linux_patches/103-dw-mipi-dsi-lpm-panel-no-hs-clock-before-init.patch b/board/batocera/rockchip/rk3326/linux_patches/103-dw-mipi-dsi-lpm-panel-no-hs-clock-before-init.patch
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..92a818bb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/board/batocera/rockchip/rk3326/linux_patches/103-dw-mipi-dsi-lpm-panel-no-hs-clock-before-init.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
+Subject: drm/bridge: dw-mipi-dsi: do not request the HS clock before an LPM panel is initialised
+
+dw_mipi_dsi_mode_set() switches to command mode for the panel's
+pre_enable/prepare through dw_mipi_dsi_set_mode(), which also asserts
+PHY_TXREQUESTCLKHS. A panel that takes its init sequence in low power
+mode over a non-continuous clock lane does not need the high speed
+clock at that point, and the XiFan RF35H panel (generic-dsi, flags
+0xe03) does not come up when it is asserted before the init sequence.
+
+For such panels only power the controller up: it is in reset from
+dw_mipi_dsi_init() and in command mode from
+dw_mipi_dsi_command_mode_config(). The clock request still happens in
+atomic_enable, once the panel is initialised. Every RK3326 panel in the
+tree (generic-dsi on eight devices, kd35t133, nv3051d, st7701) declares
+MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM and MIPI_DSI_CLOCK_NON_CONTINUOUS, so this is the
+path they all take; it is the sequence the RF35H has been booting with
+on other distributions.
+
+--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-mipi-dsi.c
++++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-mipi-dsi.c
+@@ -1019,8 +1019,23 @@
+ 
+ 	dw_mipi_dsi_wait_for_two_frames(adjusted_mode);
+ 
+-	/* Switch to cmd mode for panel-bridge pre_enable & panel prepare */
+-	dw_mipi_dsi_set_mode(dsi, 0);
++	/*
++	 * Switch to cmd mode for panel-bridge pre_enable & panel prepare.
++	 *
++	 * A panel that takes its init sequence in low power mode over a
++	 * non-continuous clock lane has no use for the high speed clock
++	 * request that dw_mipi_dsi_set_mode() asserts here, and some
++	 * (XiFan RF35H) do not come up when it is asserted before they are
++	 * initialised: the controller is still in reset from
++	 * dw_mipi_dsi_init() and in command mode from
++	 * dw_mipi_dsi_command_mode_config(), so power it up and leave the
++	 * clock request to atomic_enable, after the panel is ready.
++	 */
++	if ((dsi->mode_flags & MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM) &&
++	    (dsi->mode_flags & MIPI_DSI_CLOCK_NON_CONTINUOUS))
++		dsi_write(dsi, DSI_PWR_UP, POWERUP);
++	else
++		dw_mipi_dsi_set_mode(dsi, 0);
+ 
+ 	if (phy_ops->power_on)
+ 		phy_ops->power_on(dsi->plat_data->priv_data);
